              "type": "text",
              "text": "<p><strong><strong>22nd - 23rd September 2026</strong></strong></p><p><strong><strong>Aircraft Cabin Air Conference 2026 (</strong></strong><a href=\"http://aircraftcabinair.com\" title=\"http://aircraftcabinair.com\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong><strong>aircraftcabinair.com</strong></strong></a><strong><strong>)</strong></strong></p><p>The International Aircraft Cabin Air Conference 2026 is an industry supported conference and essential two-day event for those seeking to understand more about the subject of contaminated air on aircraft, the operational aspects and the cabin environment.</p><p>The conference, through a drinks reception and an optional conference delegates dinner event provides excellent networking opportunities. The conference is the leading conference in the world on the issue and follows on from the previous 2005, 2017, 2019, 2021, 2023 and 2024 conferences held.</p><p>The 2026 conference will discuss new jet engine oils, recent research findings and challenges faced by aircraft operators, engineers and air crew. It will also present the solutions emerging for airframers, airlines and aircraft operators such as air cleaning technologies. Additionally, the flight safety implications, the aircraft environment, latest air monitoring data and sensor technology, legal cases, media exposure, medical aspects and much more, will also be presented.</p><p>Join us for two days with over 30 expert speakers to map the business, medical aspects, regulatory, safety and technical solutions to cabin air contamination. The International Aircraft Cabin Air Conference 2026 will be the most in-depth conference ever held on this topic.</p><p>Based on feedback from previous conferences, the delegates drinks reception at the end of the first day (Tuesday 22nd September 2026), will be extended further. This is to provide furthermore networking oppertunities in a relaxing environment to create vibrant and meaningful discussions, and valuable connections.</p><p><strong><strong>Lunch, drinks reception and refreshments are included in the conference pass. The optional conference delegates dinner at the prestigious Royal Air Force Club, is an extra that MUST be booked at the same time as booking a delegates pass.</strong></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Prices</strong></strong></p><p><strong><strong>Full Price 2 Day Conference Admission including lunch and drinks reception: </strong></strong>£525.00 (+ taxes &amp; booking fee) ** SAME PRICE AS IN 2019**</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Academia Discount Rate: </strong></strong>Please contact operations@aircraftcabinair.com for discount code</p><p><em><em>Limited tickets available. Book early to avoid disappointment.</em></em></p><p><br></p>",
